    question_en: "AeroVista Regional operates a flight reservation and check-in platform hosted on a fleet of Amazon EC2 instances within an Auto Scaling group behind an Application Load Balancer. During a high-traffic promotional fare campaign, multiple EC2 instances became unresponsive and customer transactions failed due to memory exhaustion caused by session caching. However, the Auto Scaling group did not scale out because the average CPU utilization remained well below the scaling threshold. A solutions architect must design an automated solution that scales out the EC2 instances when memory utilization exceeds 75% and notifies the operations team when this occurs.\n\nWhich solution meets these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?",
