    question_en: "A healthcare records startup is building an automated analytics pipeline on AWS to analyze anonymized patient encounter summaries and clinical billing logs. Partner clinics upload CSV files containing these records to an Amazon S3 bucket multiple times each day. The files must be ingested and processed automatically within minutes of upload. Healthcare analysts will then query this data to build business intelligence (BI) dashboards and perform complex analytical queries that involve multi-table joins and aggregations across terabytes of historical patient encounter data.\n\nA solutions architect must design a solution that meets these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead.\n\nWhich solution should the solutions architect recommend?",
